Carafe: with IndirectCallCache, an indirect call keeps the first target it reaches. The call site gets a record of
the guest target and its host code after the block's jump thunks; a call to the same target loads the host code from
the record instead of hashing into the L1 lookup table, and other targets take the lookup as before. An empty record
sends the call through a dispatcher stub that finds or compiles the target, fills the record once and registers a
block link whose delinker clears it when the target's code goes. Off by default.
MIT, as the files it changes.

